WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.340
November is the perfect month for long nights
at home with your TV, and Amazon is delivering

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.620
plenty of entertainment to keep you occupied.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:12.219
From Jack Ryan and James Bond to Christmas
comedies and Hollywood classics, here are

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:15.800
some fresh new arrivals coming to Amazon Prime
in November.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:21.500
If you're a James Bond fan and an Amazon Prime
Video subscriber, you're going to be very

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.680
pleased with the streaming service this November.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:24.980
"Mr…?"

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:26.380
"Bond.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:28.860
James Bond."

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:34.100
Throughout November, Prime's action offerings
will be largely dominated by a certain Agent

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:34.940
007.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:41.320
Beginning with 1962's Dr. No and ending with
2002's Die Another Day, nearly the entire

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:46.280
James Bond film library will be available
for streaming on Amazon Prime Video on November

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:46.960
1st.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:51.580
Unfortunately, the additions don't include
any of Daniel Craig's more recent entries,

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:56.300
or the 1967 spoof Casino Royale, but everything
else will be there.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:00.560
Unless Daniel Craig is your favorite Bond,
you should be very pleased indeed.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:05.460
Settle in and catch up on all the entries
starring Sean Connery, Roger Moore, Timothy

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.020
Dalton, and Pierce Brosnan.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:12.860
Oh, and George Lazenby's sole contribution,
1969's On Her Majesty's Secret Service, will

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:13.740
be there, too.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.260
The name is Marathon.

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:17.200
James Bond Marathon.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:23.280
Most viewers know John Krasinski for his portrayal
of Jim Halpert on The Office, and they might

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.270
have a tough time buying him as the star of
a political thriller.

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:28.000
Well, let's not be that way.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.720
The first season of Jack Ryan earned plenty
of positive reviews, and Krasinski already

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.480
proved he's a versatile actor with A Quiet
Place.

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:40.340
On November 1st, fans will get their second
chance to see Krasinski fight against terrorism,

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.820
political corruption, and everything in between.

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:47.420
Jack Ryan's first season had lots of globe-hopping
between the States, Europe, and the Middle

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:47.920
East.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:50.440
But for the second season, things are going
south.

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:55.780
Ryan travels to South America to investigate
illegal arms sales in the Venezuelan jungle.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:01.200
His investigation eventually uncovers a vast
conspiracy involving a corrupt Venezuelan

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:05.650
president, secret dealings with Russia, and
the possibility of Venezuela getting its hands

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:06.880
on nuclear weapons.

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:08.459
"We do this, we do this together."

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:09.560
"I can live with that."

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:16.219
Amazon Prime Video added lots of horror movies
at the end of September in preparation for

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:16.940
Halloween.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:21.620
So if you're tired of the scares, the blood,
and the gore, too bad, because more is on

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:22.300
the way.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:27.800
On November 1st, Tim Burton's 2007 adaptation
of the stage musical Sweeney Todd: The Demon

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:30.120
Barber of Fleet Street starts streaming.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:36.299
It stars Johnny Depp as a serial killer-slash-barber
in 19th-century London, who murders his customers

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.640
with palpable glee.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:42.760
Meanwhile, his fiendish co-conspirator, played
by Helena Bonham Carter, turns the dead bodies

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:46.520
into tasty meat pies and feeds them to unsuspecting
customers.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.180
It's deliciously good fun.

00:02:48.189 --> 00:02:53.250
If you're still hungry for more abject terror,
the classic 2002 horror film The Ring starts

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:57.820
streaming the same day, and it revolves around
a cursed videotape that kills whoever watches

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:58.320
it.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:06.660
"Seven days!"

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:14.120
If you're looking for even more gore, prepare
yourself for the 2013 horror film Texas Chainsaw,

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:16.620
which will be showing up on Prime on November
6th.

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:21.760
And if you're on the hunt for more classic
terror, be sure to track down the 1987 thriller

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.940
Fatal Attraction, which begins streaming on
November 1st.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:31.060
Glenn Close stars as Alex, a wildly unhinged
woman whose infatuation with a married man,

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:34.440
played by Michael Douglas, quickly takes a
turn for the psychotic.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:38.760
After they share a passionate weekend together,
this very married man tries to move on with

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:39.560
his life.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:44.180
Well, that doesn't go over too well, particularly
for an ill-fated pet rabbit.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:46.420
"Daddy?"

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:47.260
"What?"

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:54.180
Close's portrayal of the psychotic spurned
lover earned her an Oscar nod - and rightfully

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:54.700
so.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:59.880
In November, Amazon Prime Video is adding
two Christmas-themed comedies that are a whole

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:02.120
lot darker than your average holiday fare.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:08.300
On November 1st, the service will start streaming
2003's Bad Santa, a highly irreverent comedy

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:12.360
that stars Billy Bob Thornton as a pitiful,
foul-mouthed mall Santa.

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:14.140
"What about the reindeer?"

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:16.300
"Would you please shut up about reindeer?"

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:22.200
Then, starting on November 13th, you can check
out the 2018 film Anna and the Apocalypse,

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:26.460
starring Ella Hunt as a woman who likes to
sing and dance while killing zombies - occasionally

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:28.480
killing them with humongous candy canes.

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:29.720
Happy holidays!

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:35.380
If you're in no mood for a holiday-themed
laugh riot, check out the 1991 comedy Soapdish

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:36.120
instead.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:41.620
This brilliant farce offers a hilarious spin
on daytime soap operas - and needless to say,

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:45.060
there's just as much drama going on behind
the scenes as in front of the camera.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:50.320
The all-star cast includes Robert Downey Jr.,
Whoopi Goldberg, Elisabeth Shue, Sally Field,

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:51.380
and many others.

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:52.720
It's really good stuff.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:57.699
One of Prime's November offerings with the
shortest turnaround time from screen to stream

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:02.540
is 2018's Creed II, the sequel to the acclaimed
2015 drama Creed.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:07.820
Michael B. Jordan plays Adonis Creed in both
films - and he's the son of the late boxer

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:10.060
Apollo Creed, played by Carl Weathers.

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:15.800
As you might recall, Apollo died fighting
a juiced-up Soviet boxer in 1985's Rocky IV.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.200
"Don't pretend this is about your father."

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:23.360
Sylvester Stallone reprises his role as Rocky
Balboa, acting as Adonis' trainer.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:29.870
The second Creed installment sees Adonis face
Viktor Drago, played by Florian Munteanu,

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:33.360
and he's the son of the man who killed Adonis's
father in the ring.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:38.820
Killer boxer Ivan Drago - played by Dolph
Lundgren - also returns to stand in his son's

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:39.320
corner.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:42.580
"He needs something to try to turn this fight
around.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:45.300
Drago just keeps coming!"

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:50.259
And if you're looking for a drama with a bit
more mystery and a way darker ending, there's

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:53.740
the classic 1974 gumshoe mystery Chinatown.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:59.200
Starring Jack Nicholson as private eye Jake
Gittes and Faye Dunaway as his client, Chinatown

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:04.060
raked in a pile of Oscar nominations, and
even nabbed a win for Best Original Screenplay.

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:09.450
In 1990, Nicholson directed a sequel, The
Two Jakes, but it wasn't nearly as well received

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:10.840
as its predecessor.

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:16.030
Chinatown is absolutely essential viewing,
so be sure to investigate this twisted mystery

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:17.140
if you haven't already.

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:19.760
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:23.900
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
TV shows and movies are coming soon.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:28.720
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

